  "description": "The 2026 election for Indiana's 1st Congressional District features incumbent Democrat Frank Mrvan facing Republican challenger Barb Regnitz. The district covers Lake and Porter counties and parts of LaPorte County in northwest Indiana, part of the Chicago metropolitan area. Mrvan has held the seat since 2021 and is seeking a fourth term, while Regnitz, a Porter County commissioner, won the Republican nomination in the May 5 primary. The race is considered competitive \u2014 the Cook Political Report rates it 'Likely Democratic' \u2014 and is viewed as one of Indiana's most closely watched congressional contests given the district's shifting political dynamics.",
